1result.sql is preferable because it

• extracts the real file‑name extension with SPLIT_PART instead of relying on broad LIKE patterns, so it won’t accidentally match strings that only contain an extension substring in the middle of the path;  
• maps extensions to languages in a single CASE expression and then drops the generic “Other”, guaranteeing that only recognised languages are counted;  
• applies the required non‑empty‑content and non‑binary filters exactly as specified;  
• still returns the same top‑10 list but with a cleaner, safer implementation.

